Why: Space lookups only where they are read: a one-window Space check asks about that window only, and the exact-target check and the running-app list skip them, so typing into an app takes about 0.1 s less with a hundred windows open.

The window server answers "which Spaces is this window on" one window at a
time (plus one more round trip for its display's current Space), so
all_windows() costs two round trips per window open on the Mac: 15-25 ms
with about a hundred windows. window_on_current_space_by_id and
window_space_view_by_id ran a whole enumeration to read one window's fields,
and gather_background_facts and list_running_apps enumerated with Space
fields they never read. One type_text into an off-Space TextEdit window ran
about five such enumerations. Results are unchanged: the one-window functions
return the same fields for that window, and the two Space-blind callers read
only ids, owners, bounds and on-screen state. Upstreamable as is.

